---
const tides = [
  ['High Tide', '6–8 cars', 'Beach Saturdays and game days.'],
  ['Half Tide', '3–4 cars', 'Weekday peaks to Metro rail.'],
  ['Low Tide', '2 cars', 'Middays and evenings.'],
  ['Slack Tide', '1 pod', 'On call at night.'],
];
const cars = [
  ['Pilot', 'The lead car and operator’s cab.'], ['Open', 'Open-air riding under a canopy.'],
  ['Quiver', 'Boards and bikes.'], ['Level', 'Step-free boarding.'], ['Galley', 'A coffee counter on the move.'],
  ['Hold', 'Cargo and everyday deliveries.'], ['Bandstand', 'A stage for a gathering.'],
  ['Tender', 'Power for the line and its stops.'], ['Seminar', 'A classroom for the University of El Segundo.'],
  ['Hush', 'A quiet car.'],
];
const credits = 'Michael Hoydich with Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Haiku 5.5, Claude Fable 5.1, ChatGPT image generation and Codex';
---
<section class="segundo-line" id="segundo-line" aria-labelledby="segundo-line-title">
  <div class="esm-wrap sl-opening">
    <p class="esm-kicker">El Segundo Motors · The Segundo Line · <a href="/b/0705">Block 0705</a></p>
    <h1 id="segundo-line-title">One pod is a ride.<br /><em>Eight pods are a train.</em></h1>
    <p class="sl-dek">El Segundo Motors' answer to “less car, more people mover”: a street train of short electric pods, each with its own motor, batteries and job, that couples into eight cars for a beach Saturday and comes apart into one pod at midnight.</p>
    <p class="sl-status">Concept; targets, not promises.</p>
    <nav class="sl-nav" aria-label="Segundo Line sections"><a href="#line-tides">The tides ↓</a><a href="#line-cars">Ten car types ↓</a><a href="#saturday-tide">Saturday Tide ↓</a><a href="https://claude.ai/artifact/M1btVPbW2yMK5tsqHqQE9Y" rel="noreferrer">Public concept microsite ↗</a></nav>
  </div>
  <div class="sl-tides" id="line-tides"><div class="esm-wrap">
    <h2>A line that follows the day.</h2>
    <p>The proposed service grows for the busy hours and gets smaller when the town is quiet.</p>
    <dl>{tides.map(([name, count, copy]) => <div><dt>{name}</dt><dd><strong>{count}</strong><span>{copy}</span></dd></div>)}</dl>
  </div></div>
  <div class="esm-wrap sl-section" id="line-cars">
    <p class="esm-kicker">Ten car types</p><h2>Each car has a job.</h2>
    <p class="sl-measure">The Line is imagined as a family of short, self-powered cars. Change the mix for the trip: a board rack for the beach, a classroom for a lesson, a quiet place for the ride home.</p>
    <ol class="sl-cars">{cars.map(([name, copy]) => <li><h3>{name}</h3><p>{copy}</p></li>)}</ol>
  </div>
  <div class="sl-operation"><div class="esm-wrap sl-operation-grid">
    <div><p class="esm-kicker">Operating principle</p><h2>No towed riders.</h2></div>
    <div><p>In the proposed design, every car drives, brakes and steers itself. Cars couple only at hubs. AI proposes the train’s size and composition; a human dispatcher approves the proposal.</p><p>This is an engineering brief, not a validated vehicle capability or a statement of road legality. Testing, accessibility review, operating permissions and insurance remain gates before any passenger service.</p></div>
  </div></div>
  <div class="esm-wrap sl-section" id="saturday-tide">
    <p class="esm-kicker">Phase 0 · Saturday Tide · summer 2027 target</p>
    <h2>Prove the riders.<br />Then build the couplers.</h2>
    <div class="sl-pilot"><div><p class="sl-lead">Four leased low-speed shuttles. Ten Saturdays. Smoky Hollow to the beach.</p><p>The proposed pilot would run as a radio-linked virtual train, with separate shuttles, before any physical coupling. Main Street and Grand Avenue are the concept route. Summer 2027 is a planning target, not a published timetable.</p><p class="sl-budget">$145k–$260k <span>concept budget, including contingency</span></p></div><div><h3>Proposed build-or-stop gates</h3><ul><li>At least 12 boardings per vehicle-hour.</li><li>Peak loads above 85% on 6 of 10 Saturdays.</li><li>30% of riders reporting that they would otherwise have driven.</li></ul><p>Couplers get built only if riders show up. If the pilot misses its demand gates, revise the service or stop the coupling program before committing to hardware.</p><p class="sl-note">These are targets in Michael’s concept, not observed results. No vehicles, funding, partners, route access or dates are booked or approved.</p></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sl-credits esm-wrap"><p class="esm-kicker">Concept by Michael Hoydich · 18 October 2026</p><p>{credits}</p><p class="sl-note">The creative process and model labels are Michael’s supplied account. They are not independently verified claims about model availability or use.</p><p><strong>Concept. Not affiliated with the City of El Segundo, LA Metro or any agency.</strong></p><div class="sl-links"><a href="https://claude.ai/artifact/M1btVPbW2yMK5tsqHqQE9Y" rel="noreferrer">Explore the public microsite ↗</a><a href="#motors-original">Continue to the original Motors case ↓</a></div></div>
</section>
<style>
  .segundo-line{background:#f4f0e5;color:#182b3c;border-bottom:1px solid #182b3c;scroll-margin-top:20px}
  .sl-opening{padding-block:68px 38px}.sl-opening h1{font:400 clamp(42px,6.5vw,92px)/1.05 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.045em;max-width:1100px;margin:22px 0 28px}.sl-opening h1 em{font-weight:400;color:#465f90}.sl-dek{max-width:870px;font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,23px);line-height:1.6}.sl-status{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #182b3c;padding:8px 12px;margin-top:22px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}
  .sl-nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 28px;border-top:1px solid #b8bdc3;margin-top:32px;padding-top:16px}.sl-nav a,.sl-links a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;font-size:13px;text-underline-offset:4px}
  .sl-tides{padding-block:44px;background:#b9c7e4;scroll-margin-top:20px}.segundo-line h2{font:400 clamp(30px,4vw,48px)/1.12 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:12px 0 22px}.sl-tides dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px;margin:30px 0 0}.sl-tides dt{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}.sl-tides dd{margin:10px 0 0}.sl-tides strong{display:block;font:400 38px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin-bottom:10px}.sl-tides dd span{display:block;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6}
  .sl-section{padding-block:58px;scroll-margin-top:18px}.sl-measure{max-width:730px}.sl-cars{list-style:none;counter-reset:car;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px 22px;padding:0;margin:35px 0 0}.sl-cars li{counter-increment:car;border-top:1px solid #182b3c;padding-top:14px}.sl-cars li::before{content:counter(car,decimal-leading-zero);font-size:11px;color:#465f90}.sl-cars h3{font:400 26px/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0}.sl-cars p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}
  .sl-operation{background:#182b3c;color:#f4f0e5;padding-block:50px}.sl-operation-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;gap:50px}.sl-operation p+p{margin-top:20px}.sl-pilot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:60px}.sl-pilot h3{font-size:16px;margin:5px 0 16px}.sl-pilot ul{padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px}.sl-lead{font-size:23px!important;line-height:1.5!important;margin-bottom:18px}.sl-budget{font:400 40px/1.2 Georgia,serif!important;margin-top:25px}.sl-budget span{display:block;font:400 12px/1.7 Inter,Arial,sans-serif;margin-top:8px}.sl-note{font-size:12px!important;line-height:1.7!important;margin-top:18px;max-width:820px}.sl-credits{padding-block:0 45px}.sl-credits>p{margin-bottom:15px}.sl-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 30px;margin-top:20px}.segundo-line a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #e06d42;outline-offset:5px}
  @media(max-width:800px){.sl-cars{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.sl-tides dl{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.sl-operation-grid,.sl-pilot{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.sl-opening{padding-top:42px}.sl-section{padding-block:42px}}
  @media(max-width:380px){.sl-cars,.sl-tides dl{gap:24px 16px}.sl-tides strong{font-size:32px}.sl-opening h1{font-size:40px}}
</style>
